    "result_text": "All 30 tests pass, `BUILD SUCCESS`, including the new `Cp19Tests` daily-limit case.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the \"reject creating an owner when 100+ owners already created today \u2192 429\" rule, following the OfficeFloor function-injection pattern already used for the per-city capacity rule.\n\n**New files:**\n- `RequireDailyOwnerLimit.java` \u2014 pipeline step that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()`; throws the checked `OwnerDailyLimitExceededException` when the count is \u2265 100. Runs before `SaveOwner`, so the count excludes the owner being created.\n- `OwnerDailyLimitExceededException.java` \u2014 checked escalation carrying the date and count.\n- `OwnerDailyLimitExceededExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` with body `{\"errors\":[\"dailyLimit\"]}`.\n- `officefloor/escalation/\u2026OwnerDailyLimitExceededException.yml` \u2014 wires the handler.\n\n**Edit:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `dailyLimit` step between `cityCapacity` and `build`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nThe existing `Cp19Tests` (creates 100 owners dated today, expects the 101st to be rejected with 429) now passes, and the full suite stays green (30/30).",
